cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GraphFlow: Visual Chart Pattern Search and Empirical Outcome Evaluation Engine"
message: "If you use GraphFlow or its statistical findings in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Yavuz"
    given-names: "Mert"
repository-code: "https://github.com/7mertyavuz/GraphFlow"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - time-series
  - dynamic-time-warping
  - technical-analysis
  - triple-barrier
  - block-bootstrap
  - multiple-hypothesis-testing
  - financial-econometrics
abstract: >-
  GraphFlow is a visual pattern search and empirical evaluation engine for
  financial time series. It pairs two-stage shape retrieval (cosine pre-filter +
  Sakoe-Chiba banded hybrid DTW/DDTW with query-derived structural, trend-line
  envelope, and two-regime impulse/consolidation signatures) with rigorous
  post-pattern outcome testing using ATR triple-barrier labeling, time-matched
  and return-matched shadow baselines, month-block bootstrap confidence
  intervals, and Bonferroni correction across 11.6 million historical windows.
